  "fun_fact": "Mushrooms are quiet climate champions — they grow on agricultural waste, need very little water or land, and their vast underground mycelium networks recycle nutrients and help lock carbon into the soil. Want to fall down the fungal rabbit hole? Shroom Sabha, a festival dedicated entirely to mushrooms, runs Sep 4–6. [Explore it →](https://shroomsabha.com/)",
